  "text": "Answer the question based on the following information.\n A robot moves on a graph sheet with X and Y-axis. The robot is moved by feeding it with a sequence of instructions. The\n different instructions that can be used in moving it, and their meanings are:\n Instruction Meaning\n   Move to point with coordinates\n GOTO\n   (x, y) no matter where you are\n (x,y)\n   currently.\n   Move parallel to the X-axis\n   through a distance of p, in the\n  WALKX(p) positive direction if p is positive,\n   and in the negative direction if p\n   is negative.\n   Move parallel to the Y-axis\n   through a distance of p, in the\n  WALKY(p) positive direction if p is positive,\n   and in the negative direction if p\n   is negative.\n The robot reaches point (6, 6) when a sequence of three instructions is executed, the first of which is a GOTO(x,y) instruction,\n the second is WALKX(2) and the third is WALKY (4). What are the value of x and y?\n A. 2, 4   B. 0, 0   C. 4, 2   D. 2, 2",
  "key": null,
