  "text": "Reasoning Puzzle Floor arrangment with family relation(Important in Sbi PO 2017).\n There are seven people A, B, C, D, E, F, G living in a building which has seven floors from (1 − 7). Out of the seven people\n living six of them belong to a family and in the family, there are two couples. Each couple lives together and has a separate\n floor and rest of them have separate floors so two floors are empty. The following information is known about them. G is the\n son-in-law of D. Neither top floor nor first floor is empty. D lives on a floor immediately below that of E. There are two floors\n between the floors on which the two couples live. C is E’s nephew and lives two floors above the floor on which B lives. A’s\n sister lives on the 3rd floor.\n Please answer it with steps or explanations. Thanks in advance",
