  "text": "The Resilience Petrochemical Refinery at Zamnagar ships the naphtha it produces by using\na group of five contracted bulk material transporters (namely KLM, SAS, ABC, SRM and KBC).\n The Resilience petrochemical refinery at Jamnagar ships the naphtha it produces by using a group of five contracted bulk\n material transporters ( namely KLM, SAS, ABC, SRM, and KBC).\n The five transporters dealt with a total of 40 millions tonnes of naphtha for the Jamnagar refinery and incurred a total cost of\n Rs. 90 million for the same.\n The first pie-chart shows the distribution of the transportation ( by tonnage ) done by the five transporters for the naphtha that\n they transported for the Jamnagar refinery.\n The second pie chart gives the break up of the total cost incurred by the five transporters for the above.\n 1. If M, N, O and P are the cost incurred per ton of the naphtha transported by SAS, KLM, KBC, and ABC respectively, the\n   correct relationship among them is\n O < N, M < P, N < P\n P > O, P < N, N < M\n M > N, P > O, N < P\n P < N, M > N, O < N\n 2. The average cost incurred per ton of naphtha transported by ABC and SRM is\n RS. 2.67\n RS. 3.01\n RS. 2.81\n RS. 1.93\n 3. Of all the options available the cheapest contracted bulk transporter is\n   a.SRM\n   b.KBC\n   c.KLM\n   d.ABC",
